<[len] NMORGENSTERN> Very good if I say so myself (and I do)
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> Back to Forth. Pascal do loops are easy to translate:
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> First define : BIGTOP 2DUP < IF SWAP THEN ;
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> This takes 2 integers, & swaps them if necessary so the
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> larger is on top. Better test it, I
   may have mixed up < and > here
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> In any case the word : FROMTO  BIGTOP 1+ SWAP ;
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> will set up Pascal or BASIC type loop parameters,
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> thus  3 6 FROMTO would give you 7 3 which would take
<[len] NMORGENSTERN> which if followed by DO would take
   the index from 3 to 6 inclusive.
